A163 — the Caddyfile's claim about the share page's own links, before and after
Host: 27.0 / arm64, caddy v2.11.4

--- BEFORE: the claim (Caddyfile, at HEAD) ---
	# Kept conversations. `/s/<id>` is a page the engine renders and it does not live under
	# `/api`, so without this block the catch-all below hands the path to the file server and
	# every share link answers 404 — which is what the shipped configuration did (A99).
	#
	# The difference from the block above is deliberate: no `header_up Host`, so Caddy passes the
	# Host it was reached on through to the engine. The engine uses that to build the page's own
	# links, which is how a link copied on a phone points back at the address the phone used
	# rather than at the engine's loopback port.

--- And the same claim inside the engine (APIServer, at HEAD) ---
        // The page's own links go back to the origin that served it, so a phone that reached the
        // page through Caddy gets Caddy's address rather than the engine's loopback port — which is
        // the address the phone could not reach in the first place (A99).

